## OpenClaw Linux appliance — package seed list (archiso profile).
##
## One package per line; blank lines and lines starting with "#" are ignored
## by mkarchiso. Comments are grouped by purpose.
##
## Every package name below was verified against the official Arch repos on
## 2026-09-03 (archlinux.org/packages/search/json, core/extra/multilib):
## re-verify before the first real ISO build (see README.md).
##
## UI note: WebKitGTK (webkit2gtk-4.1) is deliberately NOT listed — it renders
## blank on the reference hardware (docs/verdicts/webkitgtk-on-beelink.md).
## All UI is Chromium app-mode or native GTK/Qt clients.
##
## mkarchiso's own boot requirements are covered in group (5): `syslinux`
## (BIOS bootloader binaries, validated by mkarchiso) and `mkinitcpio-archiso`
## (the initramfs hooks that make the live media find and mount its root).

# (1) Base system + kernel
base
linux
linux-firmware
intel-ucode          # reference hardware is Alder Lake-N (Intel)
networkmanager       # network control (nmcli/nmtui)
openssh              # remote management of the appliance
sudo                 # admin user for the appliance desktop session

# (2) Hyprland-family desktop (minimal bar + terminal; matches the beelink reference box)
hyprland
foot                 # Wayland-native terminal
waybar               # minimal status bar
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
brightnessctl        # backlight control (laptop/appliance displays)
wl-clipboard         # Wayland clipboard (needed by Chromium app-mode)
# X11 compatibility + desktop plumbing
xorg-xwayland        # X11 fallback for non-Wayland clients
polkit               # privilege prompts for desktop apps
xdg-utils            # xdg-open & friends
# Audio (PipeWire stack)
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
# Fonts
noto-fonts

# (3) UI runtime: Chromium app-mode
# The OpenClaw dashboard/pairing UI runs as `chromium --app=...` (see
# provision/install-dashboard-launcher.sh). Do NOT add webkit2gtk-4.1 here.
chromium

# (4) OpenClaw gateway runtime
git
nodejs
pnpm
base-devel           # build toolchain for AUR/from-source additions

# (5) Boot/install plumbing
# Live-media boot chain: syslinux (BIOS bootloader binaries mkarchiso copies
# into the ISO) and mkinitcpio-archiso (archiso initramfs hooks, used when
# mkinitcpio builds initramfs-linux.img inside the build chroot).
syslinux
mkinitcpio-archiso
# Installed-target boot (EFI, Intel reference box): grub + efibootmgr for
# the post-install bootloader setup; dosfstools for FAT/EFI work.
grub
efibootmgr
dosfstools
